 2. A dose of separation 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Sarah Grillo/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 CVS is splitting in two, announcing plans today to spin off its retail pharmacy business in 2028.

 The spin would house the company's 9,000 pharmacies, medical clinic and mail pharmacy businesses. CVS Health would retain its Aetna insurance operation, Caremark pharmacy benefit manager, and specialty pharmacy and health care services businesses. 📉 The impact: Shares closed down 12.5%

 🔍 The big picture: CVS is betting the breakup will bring greater operational agility as it rethinks the integrated health care model it spent years building, Axios Pro Deals' Brock E.W. Turner writes .

 The move also provides some proactive cover from mounting antitrust scrutiny. Regulatory heat on CVS has intensified over the past 18 months, primarily over its pharmacy benefit practices and vertically integrated business model. Go deeper , with Axios Pro Deals .

 
 
