 4. 🕔 After hours: To live and die 
 
 By Dan Primack and Nathan Bomey 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Bryson DeChambeau at a LIV Golf tournament in August. Photo: Justin Casterline/Getty Images

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Efforts to keep the LIV Golf league alive have collapsed.

 BC Partners — which had tentatively agreed to invest in a "LIV 2.0" league — is walking away, a source familiar with the matter confirmed today. The league was unable to secure enough support in time to meet the deadlines set in the bankruptcy case. 🏌 Between the lines: At least 30 players ultimately indicated interest in signing on, the source tells us, but economic terms remained a sticking point with some of their representatives.

 What's next: People involved in the case expect LIV to pivot to a liquidation.

